{"nodes": [{"id": "agents_dead_drop_runtime", "label": "dead-drop transport-agnostic runtime", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Applications on different machines talk through infrastructure they already share (git repo, synced folder, object storage) so neither side must listen on a public port."}, {"id": "agents_npm_workspace_two_packages", "label": "Two-package npm workspace", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "lines 7, 29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TypeScript throughout with zero runtime dependencies outside the workspace; layers are directories rather than packages so layering is enforced by lint rather than package boundaries."}, {"id": "agents_npm_run_verify", "label": "npm run verify (the gate)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "lines 15, 23", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lint, build and tests with coverage thresholds must pass before a change is done; CI additionally runs format:check, the three examples and the whole suite on Windows, so passing only on macOS is not finished."}, {"id": "agents_npm_test", "label": "npm test", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 16", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_npm_run_build", "label": "npm run build (tsc --build)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_npm_run_format", "label": "npm run format / format:check", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "lines 18-19", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_conformance_example", "label": "custom-transport conformance example (19/19 cases)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 20", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_git_binary_requirement", "label": "git binary required, no network or credentials", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 25", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_packages_transport_sdk", "label": "packages/transport-sdk", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 33", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The contract third parties compile against, plus the conformance suite; versioned independently so an adapter written today keeps working across dead-drop majors."}, {"id": "agents_layer_protocol", "label": "protocol layer", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 34", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defines what a message is (envelope, framing, encryption, chunking, errors) and holds zero policy, so policy churn cannot break the wire contract."}, {"id": "agents_layer_core", "label": "core layer", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 35", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All policy lives here: mailbox engine, transport manager, retry, breaker, dedupe, observability."}, {"id": "agents_layer_runtime", "label": "runtime layer", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 36", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Workspaces, exposures, discovery, plugin loading, control plane."}, {"id": "agents_layer_sdk", "label": "sdk layer", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 37", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Client over the control socket."}, {"id": "agents_layer_cli", "label": "cli layer (ddrop command)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 38", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_transports_directory", "label": "src/transports/* (filesystem, git, github, memory)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 39", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_test_tree_convention", "label": "Tests mirror src, never live in src", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "lines 40-41", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every layering rule scopes itself to src/, so keeping tests out of src/ is what makes tests exempt from layering restrictions."}, {"id": "agents_e2e_scenario_suite", "label": "e2e scenario suite (run.sh, lib.sh, fast/ and live/)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_adr_directory", "label": "docs/adr decision records", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "lines 43, 72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Anything that deviates from docs/vision.md gets a record explaining what was rejected and why."}, {"id": "agents_layering_enforcement", "label": "Layering enforced by no-restricted-imports", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 45", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Direction is protocol <- core <- runtime <- {sdk, cli}, enforced by eslint inside one package rather than by package boundaries. Two documented exceptions: runtime/plugins.ts owns the transport table, and the github transport delegates to git."}, {"id": "agents_subpath_exports", "label": "Layer subpath exports of @fyrlabs/dead-drop", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 45", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agents_invariant_no_transport_naming", "label": "Invariant 1: nothing above the transport manager may name a transport", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 49", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If application code could ask for 'the GitHub one', transport independence would be a slogan rather than a property."}, {"id": "agents_invariant_two_transport_kinds", "label": "Invariant 2: two transport kinds, store and native", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 50", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Adapters implement put/get/list/delete (store) or send/subscribe (native); adding send/receive to the store contract is forbidden. See ADR 0001."}, {"id": "agents_invariant_control_plane_socket", "label": "Invariant 3: control plane is a Unix socket mode 0600 or a Windows named pipe, never TCP", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 51", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "See ADR 0003; a TCP control plane would expose runtime control beyond local filesystem permissions."}, {"id": "agents_invariant_delivery_guarantee", "label": "Invariant 4: at-least-once delivery, best-effort ordering per recipient", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 52", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No doc or comment may claim a stronger guarantee than the system actually provides."}, {"id": "agents_invariant_message_id_is_trace_id", "label": "Invariant 5: a message id is its trace id", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 53", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "workspace.request, mailbox.send and mailbox.deliver key their span to the envelope id, a response using its correlationId, which is what makes `ddrop trace <requestId>` work with the id a timeout error already returns."}, {"id": "agents_invariant_transport_imports", "label": "Invariant 6: built-in transports may import only node builtins or declared dependencies", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 54", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Workspaces are hoisted, so a module that loads in this repo can be missing from a real install. Enforced by test/transport-imports.test.ts; it went unguarded for several releases because the enforcing test was named after packages/cli and did not survive the consolidation."}, {"id": "agents_invariant_sdk_only_public_contract", "label": "Invariant 7: transport-sdk is the only stable public contract", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 55", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It is the one thing outside this repository that must keep working across releases, so changing it is a breaking change."}, {"id": "agents_invariant_no_bridge_name", "label": "Invariant 8: never reintroduce the name Bridge", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 56", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The old `bridge` binary collided with iproute2's bridge(8) on Linux. Checked with an rg command that must print nothing; only AGENTS.md and the release checklist may contain the word because they state the rule."}, {"id": "agents_invariant_hostile_storage", "label": "Invariant 9: the transport is hostile storage for frame contents", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every frame is ciphertext including the envelope header, so no envelope field may leak a channel, peer or workspace name in clear text. Object keys are the deliberate exception so an operator can look at a git repo and understand it; a 0.1.0 release note claimed names never appear in clear text and was simply false."}, {"id": "agents_invariant_error_symbol_brand", "label": "Invariant 10: DeadDropError identity is a registry symbol, never instanceof", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 58", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DeadDropError.is brand-checks Symbol.for('@fyrlabs/dead-drop.DeadDropError') so it holds when two copies of transport-sdk land in one dependency tree. With instanceof, a third-party adapter's non-retryable error would be re-wrapped by DeadDropError.from as INTERNAL, which is retryable, and the retry loop would hammer a permanent failure. The same reasoning forbids an exact-version pin on transport-sdk."}, {"id": "agents_commit_convention", "label": "Angular commit convention", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 62", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "type(scope): subject, imperative and lowercase, no trailing period; body explains what and why, not how; breaking changes use ! or a BREAKING CHANGE footer; one commit per completed logical unit, not one per session."}, {"id": "agents_test_philosophy", "label": "A test that would have caught the bug beats a test that covers the fix", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 64", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three real defects were caught this way and each is noted in the commit that fixed it. Coverage thresholds are 80% and sit near 90%, but coverage is a floor, not a goal."}, {"id": "agents_clock_injection", "label": "Injected Clock, never Date.now or bare timers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 66", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The injected clock lets retry and backoff suites run in milliseconds instead of sleeping."}, {"id": "agents_deaddroperror", "label": "DeadDropError with stable code and honest retryable flag", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 68", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The transport manager reads `retryable` to decide between retrying and failing over, so getting the flag wrong causes real misbehaviour."}, {"id": "agents_docs_in_same_commit", "label": "Docs change in the same commit as behaviour", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 70", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "docs/configuration.md is expected to match runtime/config.ts field for field, and anything user-visible gets a CHANGELOG entry under Unreleased."}, {"id": "agents_windows_trap", "label": "Windows path and named-pipe trap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never compare a resolved path against an unresolved one and never assume / separators. Two Windows-only CI failures happened here; the second was in a test whose helper bound its own control socket without taking the named-pipe branch defaultSocketPath takes, because listen on a socket path fails there with a bare EACCES that names nothing."}, {"id": "agents_hoisting_trap", "label": "Workspace hoisting hides missing dependencies", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every workspace package resolves from the repo root, so check manifests, not just imports."}, {"id": "agents_prettier_rename_trap", "label": "Renaming a symbol can reflow unrelated files", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Identifier length changes reflow lines and fail format:check in untouched files, so run npm run format after any large rename."}, {"id": "agents_bin_path_trap", "label": "npm bin path must not start with ./", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A ./ prefix makes npm warn that the entry was invalid and removed; write dist/bin.js."}, {"id": "agents_socket_path_length_cap", "label": "defaultSocketPath and the 104-byte Unix socket cap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 80", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Past 104 bytes defaultSocketPath falls back to a hashed path under the temp directory; a raw join(dataDir, ...) is reachable from the documented quick start and bind fails with a bare EINVAL."}, {"id": "agents_git_push_exit_code_trap", "label": "git push exit 0 is not proof anything was published", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 81", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "push prints 'Everything up-to-date' and exits 0 when HEAD no longer carries the commit, which happens whenever a second process shares the clone, and ddrop connect starts its own runtime from the same config. The git transport checks merge-base --is-ancestor <commit> origin/<branch> instead; a live GitHub run lost 10 of 50 requests to the exit-code version."}, {"id": "agents_git_rev_parse_trap", "label": "git rev-parse --git-dir answers for the enclosing repository", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 82", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It exits 0 anywhere under a checkout, so using it to decide whether workDir is already this transport's clone made a nested workDir read the user's own project as the clone: initialise repointed origin, rewrote user.name/user.email and checked out an orphan branch over their work. Ask whether <workDir>/.git exists; a --show-toplevel path comparison also fails because the macOS temp directory is a symlink."}, {"id": "agents_workdir_holds_no_bookkeeping", "label": "A git working tree holds no dead-drop bookkeeping", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 83", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "git add --all stages everything under the prefix and walk lists everything that is not .git or README.md, so anything placed inside workDir is committed to the data branch and served as an object. The ownership lock and extra clones live beside workDir as <workDir>.owner and <workDir>.peers/; putting either inside broke checkout for every other clone twice."}, {"id": "agents_version_from_manifest", "label": "VERSION reads the package manifest, never a literal", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 84", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A hard-coded literal in cli/cli.ts went stale and shipped a CLI reporting the wrong version in --version, status and /health. A test asserting CLI output equals VERSION does not catch it; assert against package.json."}, {"id": "agents_independent_package_versions", "label": "The two packages do not share a version", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 88", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "transport-sdk is the stable contract and moves rarely; @fyrlabs/dead-drop depends on it by caret range and churns freely. The release workflow skips whichever package is already on the registry at its manifest version, and the tag name tracks @fyrlabs/dead-drop."}, {"id": "agents_no_exact_version_pin", "label": "Never pin transport-sdk to an exact version", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 90", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DeadDropError identity depends on one copy of transport-sdk being installed, and an exact pin forces a second copy into any tree that also holds a third-party adapter."}, {"id": "agents_release_autonomy", "label": "Releasing does not need permission", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 94", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Version numbers are cheap; a broken artifact on the registry is not, because a published version can never be reused. Publish verified work rather than leaving it waiting to be asked about."}, {"id": "agents_tag_is_not_a_release", "label": "A tag is not a release", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 96", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "release.yml publishes when a GitHub release is published, so tags are cheap and reversible: pushing vX.Y.Z marks a candidate, gh release create is what puts it on npm, and a bad candidate is simply never released."}, {"id": "agents_live_github_walkthrough", "label": "Live GitHub walkthrough before tagging", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 92", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Everything GitHub-specific is otherwise tested only against a scripted fake gh."}, {"id": "agents_throwaway_test_repos", "label": "Throwaway private GitHub repos for testing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 98", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fine to create without asking and to leave behind; deleting them needs a delete_repo scope that is deliberately not granted, which is why e2e/run.sh live takes the repository as an argument."}, {"id": "docs_architecture", "label": "docs/architecture.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 9", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Read before changing anything structural: it explains the layering and what each layer is forbidden to know."}, {"id": "docs_security_model", "label": "docs/security-model.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_vision", "label": "docs/vision.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_configuration", "label": "docs/configuration.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": "line 70", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id":